<title>UK: BOE revises money market shortage to 100 mln stg.</title>
<headline>BOE revises money market shortage to 100 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it revised down its forecast money market shortage to 100 million stg.</p>
<p>Having provided 100 million stg assistance after 1100 GMT, there is no residual shortage left. The Bank said discount houses had made no us of the late repo facility by 1350 GMT.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
